# SYNTAX TEST "text.html.tiddlywiki5" "Inline rules, read from TiddlyWiki's own matchRegExp"

Two --dashes and three ---dashes.
#   ^^ text.html.tiddlywiki5 meta.paragraph.tiddlywiki5 constant.character.dash.ndash.tiddlywiki5
#                      ^^^ text.html.tiddlywiki5 meta.paragraph.tiddlywiki5 constant.character.dash.mdash.tiddlywiki5

One -dash and four ----dashes read as text.
#   ^^^^^ text.html.tiddlywiki5 meta.paragraph.tiddlywiki5
#                  ^^^^^^^^^^ text.html.tiddlywiki5 meta.paragraph.tiddlywiki5

Entities &amp; and &#38; and &#x26; here.
#         ^^^ text.html.tiddlywiki5 meta.paragraph.tiddlywiki5 constant.character.entity.named.amp.html.tiddlywiki5
#                   ^^^^ text.html.tiddlywiki5 meta.paragraph.tiddlywiki5 constant.character.entity.numeric.decimal.html.tiddlywiki5
#                             ^^^^^ text.html.tiddlywiki5 meta.paragraph.tiddlywiki5 constant.character.entity.numeric.hexadecimal.html.tiddlywiki5

Too short &a; and too long &abcdefghij; read as ambiguous.
#         ^ text.html.tiddlywiki5 meta.paragraph.tiddlywiki5 invalid.illegal.ambiguous-ampersand.html.tiddlywiki5
#                          ^ text.html.tiddlywiki5 meta.paragraph.tiddlywiki5 invalid.illegal.ambiguous-ampersand.html.tiddlywiki5

Code `one` and ``two`` here.
#     ^^^ text.html.tiddlywiki5 meta.paragraph.tiddlywiki5 markup.inline.raw.single.tiddlywiki5
#                ^^^ text.html.tiddlywiki5 meta.paragraph.tiddlywiki5 markup.inline.raw.double.tiddlywiki5

A link [[Caption|Target]] here.
#        ^^^^^^^ text.html.tiddlywiki5 meta.paragraph.tiddlywiki5 markup.link.tiddlywiki5 string.entity.other.title.link.tiddlywiki5
#                ^^^^^^ text.html.tiddlywiki5 meta.paragraph.tiddlywiki5 markup.link.tiddlywiki5 markup.underline.link.tiddlywiki5

A transclusion {{Title||Template}} here.
#                       ^^^^^^^^ text.html.tiddlywiki5 meta.paragraph.tiddlywiki5 meta.transclusion.transcludeinline.tiddlywiki5 entity.name.other.tiddler.title.template.tiddlywiki5

An external https://example.com/a here.
#           ^^^^^ text.html.tiddlywiki5 meta.paragraph.tiddlywiki5 markup.underline.link.external.tiddlywiki5 markup.underline.link.external.https.tiddlywiki5

An unknown scheme zzz://example.com/a reads as text.
#                 ^^^ text.html.tiddlywiki5 meta.paragraph.tiddlywiki5

A system link $:/core/ui/Thing here.
#                ^^^^^^^^^^^^^ text.html.tiddlywiki5 meta.paragraph.tiddlywiki5 markup.underline.link.syslink.tiddlywiki5

# TiddlyWiki ships CamelCase linking DISABLED (core/wiki/config/wikilink.tid, PR #7513), so
# the construct reads under `meta.`, which 4 of 45 bundled themes paint, rather than under
# `markup.underline.link.`, which 31 of them do. The scope still names the construct, so a
# reader who enables CamelCase in their wiki colours it in one settings rule.
A CamelCaseLink and a ~SuppressedLink here.
# ^^^^^^^^^^^^^ text.html.tiddlywiki5 meta.paragraph.tiddlywiki5 meta.link.wikilink.tiddlywiki5
# ^ - markup.underline.link.wikilink.tiddlywiki5
#                     ^ text.html.tiddlywiki5 meta.paragraph.tiddlywiki5 meta.link.wikilink.tiddlywiki5 punctuation.definition.suppress.wikilink.tiddlywiki5

An image [img[alt|file.png]] here.
#         ^^^ text.html.tiddlywiki5 meta.paragraph.tiddlywiki5 markup.other.image.tiddlywiki5 keyword.other.img.tiddlywiki5
#                 ^^^^^^^^ text.html.tiddlywiki5 meta.paragraph.tiddlywiki5 markup.other.image.tiddlywiki5 markup.underline.link.image.tiddlywiki5

Styled @@color:red;text@@ here.
#                  ^^^^ text.html.tiddlywiki5 meta.paragraph.tiddlywiki5 markup.other.style.tiddlywiki5
